{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/card-sync.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731057Z","id":"487dd91624f77a276deb8f3ecfe7963392c43620da67d0e2082724611e817b40","body":{"detail":"The gallery topic is shared by every viewer, so it cannot carry this viewer's attention (addressed threads, new replies, open threads): a version, thread or thread_deleted event there still fetches the viewer's attention on that one artifact, and a card's roster (participants) is only as fresh as the last full fetch (going live, resync, and every SAFETY_MS).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"7bdd3932434a71d1ad19e2be45e3bcc78fc1aeb1b9b1eb6f901e3465908a0ac1"},"suggested_fix":"A per-viewer topic, or attention computed from the thread summary, would remove the fetch.","summary":"The gallery fetches this viewer's attention per event","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:28.381871Z","id":"4708b4264803165869b7e2a20709b0ed80f387495339ea5ebb29e18a5f66abbb","body":{"detail":"InboxPage moved out of the q module (web/shell/src/q/index.ts) into its own chunk, imported by web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts inboxPage() and started beside q() in loadQ, so the questions budget (web/perf/bundle-budget.json, 16384; now 14202) has room for the multi-question card. The two imports run in parallel, so no request waits on another, but web/perf/usable.perf.ts has no /inbox gate to show the time to usable is unchanged.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":47},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"5db66b848687622e5d49e34f29d62226d5e43b73a103486a2ad57576b2d27af4"},"suggested_fix":"Add an /inbox first-usable measurement to web/perf/usable.perf.ts.","summary":"/inbox now loads its page as a chunk of its own beside the q module, and no perf gate times /inbox","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewComment.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:00:38.378103Z","id":"753891e2ec0c63c60fad14a86220781e7be5f417335ad46c5fb85568d52ca61c","body":{"detail":"The box re-implements the stage composer's target line, status line, focus on render, Escape to close, Cmd/Ctrl+Enter to post and the busy state (Composer.svelte). Rendering Composer.svelte from this lazy chunk makes the artifact entry export it, which adds 5 gzip bytes to an entry that sits exactly at its budget (63988 in web/perf/bundle-budget.json, measured by web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs). A behaviour change to the stage composer (a post queued while a screenshot is taken, the keyboard-trail guard, the live status region) must be mirrored here by hand.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"072d1faa169ad8499be271406d7ad89a490cbb4a88f0a1450fc3c964f840da26"},"suggested_fix":"Render Composer.svelte here once the artifact entry has a few bytes of slack, or move Composer.svelte's form into a component both import.","summary":"The New comment box repeats Composer.svelte's form instead of rendering it","tags":["revisit:the artifact entry has slack under its bundle budget","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:00:38.378379Z","id":"ae1c646c0ce8c2a549174efa8143c36778006cb14a64451371ca253ef652f4e5","body":{"detail":"The panel's first child stays the questions slot (shell/src/sidebar.test.ts 'puts the questions about the page at the top' asserts it), so an agent's question to the viewer still leads; the box comes next, above the working strips, the batch-send button and every thread. Putting the box first means changing that rule and its test.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":196},"end":{"line":201},"content_hash":"fef8ce9785f9ab52019fb078c2e7a3d70f61d7555644dc6354c03c421220d211"},"summary":"The New comment box sits below the questions for the viewer, not first in the panel","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewComment.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:10:14.562354Z","id":"a1183f70422a18f50596fd21afab39b387b08d9efb06a2812ce2fcf243100d3f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ffd6520","summary":"NewComment.svelte now renders Composer.svelte with wholeDraft(); the artifact entry's budget rose by the 18 gzip bytes this costs (63988 to 64006). Evidence: `npx vitest run shell/src/new-comment.test.ts` passes (6 tests, the composer opened in place), `node scripts/bundle-size.mjs` passes at artifact 64006, and e2e/whole-comment.spec.ts passes.","supersedes":"753891e2ec0c63c60fad14a86220781e7be5f417335ad46c5fb85568d52ca61c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:10:14.562538Z","id":"34e47162a05b76ffccf89f11259da17f6f73e72bedf6bea858a49095e6fad068","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Decided by the coordinator of this work: the box stays below the questions slot, since questions to the viewer are time-sensitive and lead the panel. No change.","supersedes":"ae1c646c0ce8c2a549174efa8143c36778006cb14a64451371ca253ef652f4e5","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T06:46:08.079116Z","id":"332f5291ec854a499f7b7a441b855187b49c34da44355e7e451dfaf2a4ac7419","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam's agent calls ask; the question reaches Sam's inbox (GET /api/inbox as Sam's cookie lists it) but Sam's shell shows 'The inbox is its owner's' at /inbox and loads no question card, so the agent waits until its timeout. Sam's shell never subscribes to the questions or inbox topic, so Hub::holds_surface for Sam is never true and every hook question of Sam's agents goes to the terminal. The server side (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs, routes/questions.rs) already serves a connected person; no plan task wires the shell for one. Plan Task 21 now carries this: gate the inbox page, the q module and the questions and inbox topics on 'owner or connected person' (a 200 from /api/inbox), verified in a real browser as a person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"4fa564c24b6a3357c8558f6fe29f63e75f25d8a83c205bb99a84e03fb763bc20"},"suggested_fix":"Gate the inbox page and the q module on 'owner or connected person' (GET /api/inbox answering 200 rather than ownerBrowser()), and verify /inbox and a question card in a real browser as a connected person.","summary":"A connected person's browser has no inbox or question surface: /inbox tells them the inbox is the owner's, and the q module loads only for the owner","tags":["review","task:21","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:40.856081Z","id":"31b2b5407e05366873abebfca2258736dba7844357defeaba91b5e1a253ee62e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"4708b4264803165869b7e2a20709b0ed80f387495339ea5ebb29e18a5f66abbb","summary":"/people now loads its page the same way (web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts peoplePage, its own chunk, measured as `people` by web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs); no perf gate times /people either.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.167408Z","id":"bb5952b279110eb432399d1781ba20bd9405c9fd6dcb56bdb085522d1da5dcce","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9cfb85d5","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"39ac376e501ae839340948c725b0c74fbe8a809c02556d58def8f9d2444bcf45"},"summary":"The inbox page, the q module and the questions and inbox topics load in any browser GET /api/inbox answers (inboxBrowser in web/shell/src/owner.ts), in the gallery and the artifact view. Evidence: gallery.test.ts 'gives a connected person's browser its inbox at /inbox, Inbox in the header, and the inbox and questions topics' passes, and e2e/inbox-cards.spec.ts passes: Sam's browser at the LAN address shows his inbox, and his answer to his agent's ask reaches the agent's clax mcp.","supersedes":"332f5291ec854a499f7b7a441b855187b49c34da44355e7e451dfaf2a4ac7419","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.168179Z","id":"b9b2cafad146ac28ee85b03a8e99ec0a102fbfe21d4bee58c39c7ec839ab8be0","body":{"detail":"InboxPage moved out of the q module (web/shell/src/q/index.ts) into its own chunk, imported by web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts inboxPage() and started beside q() in loadQ, so the questions budget (web/perf/bundle-budget.json, 16384; now 14202) has room for the multi-question card. The two imports run in parallel, so no request waits on another, but web/perf/usable.perf.ts has no /inbox gate to show the time to usable is unchanged.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"8562287422b69247ef5172e2996d8000dd4a834547e2eec0f95c600f71de4284"},"suggested_fix":"Add an /inbox first-usable measurement to web/perf/usable.perf.ts.","summary":"/inbox now loads its page as a chunk of its own beside the q module, and no perf gate times /inbox","supersedes":"4708b4264803165869b7e2a20709b0ed80f387495339ea5ebb29e18a5f66abbb","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.815322Z","id":"a41a081a026386a88b9b7c4791858f7a18e9136c79a6a73c6f7927b13532f26d","body":{"detail":"The card is shown while the thread's delivery state is withheld; deciding releases the thread, so the card (and the outcome it shows, \"Allowed in this thread\") disappears with the next thread event, and the label changes to the delivery state. The inbox keeps decided cards in place.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"34910f9acc7a57e27bfa368560c2dc444964520c59d09eb71bf5bf41d06e0e87"},"suggested_fix":"Keep a card decided here until the thread is collapsed or the view reloads.","summary":"The approval card above a thread leaves as soon as the decision lands","tags":["task:22","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.162875Z","id":"51447d801fa5818c946632cf7853a6ab0eb7ba16df2e9fbe17d7a07284da5860","body":{"detail":"Failure: a LAN viewer comments on a thread, the owner replies '+1', and the owner sends the thread to Sam's agent (Sam lets the owner's content reach his agents). Sam gets an open routing request for the LAN viewer's comment (GET /api/approvals/requests) and his inbox strip says '2 approvals' for two such threads, but the thread's feedback_state is 'sent': the owner's card reads 'sent, waiting for the agent' and Sam's artifact view shows no approval card above the thread, because the card is gated on feedback_state.state === 'withheld' (here) and the daemon derives that state from the thread's latest forwarded comment only (FEEDBACK_STATES, crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:1800-1822). Reproduced in Chromium on a scratch daemon at commit f7a89d53.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"34910f9acc7a57e27bfa368560c2dc444964520c59d09eb71bf5bf41d06e0e87"},"suggested_fix":"Show the card for every open thread with an open approval item for this viewer (thread-approvals.ts already fetches them per artifact), not only withheld ones; and have the thread's delivery state read withheld (with its approver) while any undelivered row of the thread is held under an open request, so the sender sees it too. Add a test with a two-comment thread whose first comment is held.","summary":"A thread whose newest comment reaches the agent hides its open approval request: no approval card above it, and its card reads 'sent, waiting for the agent'","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.163617Z","id":"da6f1bf933685f5439c5ccd642c822204ec8e5b31c5a84fb265ce2250a6b7a12","body":{"detail":"The chip is capped at 45% of the card head with an ellipsis; a 32-character agent name ('clax-multi-person-agent-strip-ab') is clipped at 1280 px, and for another person's agent the person after ' · ' is not visible at all at 390 px, where there is no hover. The title is only '<person>'s agent', so the clipped agent name cannot be read anywhere on the card.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"c4e0c89012c6eee44bb22a89549c9a94d4af865540ab76a4a3f1e6175bbff523"},"suggested_fix":"Make the title '<agent name>, <person>'s agent' (or 'your agent'), so hover and assistive tech get the whole name.","summary":"The owner chip's hover text never names the agent, and the chip clips both name and person","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.255042Z","id":"1bd4ebd4d659cd4ddb42d8f9957736b3bf60aa09f9814cc57131b7b9cdf29ad3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"The thread's state reads withheld while any of its rows is held (state_of in crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs looks at every row, not only the newest comment's), and the sidebar puts the approval card above any sent thread with an open request of this viewer's, whatever its state. Evidence: api_approvals::a_thread_waits_for_approval_while_an_earlier_comment_is_held passes (LAN viewer comments, the owner replies '+1', the owner sends to Sam's agent: one request, state withheld, approver Sam), and fails with the old newest-comment-only check; thread-owner.test.ts 'puts the card above a thread whose newest comment went through while an earlier one waits' passes.","supersedes":"51447d801fa5818c946632cf7853a6ab0eb7ba16df2e9fbe17d7a07284da5860","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.257609Z","id":"cbe7729e9446a4831c5098169e7d9b1bb1ce82b0a84fd3a26218b148c6e02a5a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"The chip's title names the agent whole: 'sam-web, Sam's agent' or 'clax-claude, your agent'. Evidence: thread-owner.test.ts chip tests and web/e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts (title 'sam-notes, Sam's agent') pass.","supersedes":"da6f1bf933685f5439c5ccd642c822204ec8e5b31c5a84fb265ce2250a6b7a12","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/thread-approvals.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.261111Z","id":"ebcdef66dfc53597bba1d8df20f8ca720898ee76046645e10c2fb56511ab2687","body":{"detail":"approvalsFor asks /api/inbox?kind=approval&artifact=<aid>&limit=200 and keeps the open ones; on an artifact with more than 200 approval items for this viewer, an older open request gets no card above its thread (the inbox still lists it).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"13ada5962992c59740f6e11d0f02bb133386432bd8365ed150f0f9331aed060c"},"suggested_fix":"Page through next_cursor, or have the inbox list filter approval items by request status.","summary":"The approval card above a thread reads the newest 200 approval items of the artifact, decided ones included","tags":["task:22","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
